  "RightSideDisplay": 10,
  "RightSideHtmlBlock": "<h4>Risk assessment matrix</h4><p>Rate the severity and probability of the mishap this move's events could cause (death or injury, environmental impact, or monetary loss). Their combination is the Risk Assessment Code (e.g. 1A = Catastrophic, Frequent). Read the risk level from Table III. Only the risk level is scored.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><th></th><th>Catastrophic (1)</th><th>Critical (2)</th><th>Marginal (3)</th><th>Negligible (4)</th></tr><tr><td>Frequent (A)</td><td>High</td><td>High</td><td>Serious</td><td>Medium</td></tr><tr><td>Probable (B)</td><td>High</td><td>High</td><td>Serious</td><td>Medium</td></tr><tr><td>Occasional (C)</td><td>High</td><td>Serious</td><td>Medium</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>Remote (D)</td><td>Serious</td><td>Medium</td><td>Medium</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>Improbable (E)</td><td>Medium</td><td>Medium</td><td>Medium</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>Eliminated (F)</td><td>Eliminated</td><td>Eliminated</td><td>Eliminated</td><td>Eliminated</td></tr></table><p>No amount of doctrine, training, warning, caution, or PPE can move a mishap probability to level F. Improbable is generally considered less than one in a million.</p><p><i>Source: MIL-STD-882E w/Change 1, Department of Defense Standard Practice: System Safety (27 September 2023), Tables I, II and III. Distribution A. Tailored definitions require formal approval under DoD Component policy.</i></p>",
